  "coverage": [
    "Native trace hiding and zero-interleaved preprocessing match the upstream production HidingFriPcs committed evaluations. Tests cover base, quadratic and cubic trace inputs, flattened extension limbs, one-row inputs, noncanonical words, and natural and bit-reversed output orders.",
    "Native quotient randomization matches upstream HidingFriPcs for quadratic and cubic quotients, every chunk in 2-, 4-, 16- and 32-way partitions, and shifts 1, 7 and 13. Independent off-domain recomposition at two points recovers the original quotient after all masks are applied.",
    "ChaCha20 draw order is preserved at an odd position crossing a counter boundary. Multi-request sampling holds the cursor lock across codeword and mask draws; concurrent aliases receive contiguous sequences. Repeated LDE generation consumes no additional randomness.",
    "The full 13.75 MiB trace LDE exceeds a 4 MiB managed budget and 1 MiB allocation limit; admitted one- and two-column tiles match the CPU DFT. Sampling and transform storage/count peaks are admitted separately before private work, and late resource pressure rejects without consuming or poisoning the stream.",
    "Downstream consumer errors and unwinds retire the shared RNG family and aliases. Existing sampler and proof-adapter failure tests remain valid.",
    "A native hidden LDE feeds a replay-salted CUDA commitment whose root matches an independent CPU Poseidon2 computation. Before audit, transfers contain only immutable public roots and the replay accepted-count status word; no random samples or intermediate polynomials cross the host boundary.",
    "Compute Sanitizer memory, race and synchronization checks cover all native tests except the intentional missing-kernel API error, plus challenger and proof-RNG adapters. Hiding kernels compile for compute_70 and compute_120.",
    "Shared hiding geometry preserves OpenCL/Metal behavior. OpenCL trace/lookup/quotient commitments, random pipelines/storage and existing scalar/quotient regressions pass, as do CPU/OpenCL builds, Apple Metal cross-compilation, standalone CUDA and streaming metadata allocation checks."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This implements polynomial-hiding primitives, not the complete native CUDA hiding PCS. Streaming commitment absorption across tiles, retained prefixes, openings/FRI, remaining proof stages, backend selection and worker/pool integration remain unfinished.",
    "No native complete-proof speedup or transaction-throughput result is claimed. The production backend, proof format, security parameters and verifier behavior are unchanged.",
    "V100 execution and Apple Metal execution remain untested on this Linux RTX 5080 host. NVRTC compilation and Metal cross-compilation are not hardware execution qualification."
  ],
  "qualification_note": "Frozen final source was rebuilt and qualified after development checks. Earlier development logs retain test-setup compilation errors and the corrected doubled-domain setup for the upstream trace PCS oracle. The first qualification controller then stopped because an added OpenCL module filter matched zero tests. The remaining controller used the corrected full module path against identical pinned source and executables, retaining all completed checks and the initial failure log; the added owned-PCS commitment checks also required explicit quotient residency and fusion/device-only selections. Initial setup failures are preserved, and the successful per-check records include the required environment. No source or binary changed between qualification phases.",
